      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's getting better, but honestly, the score is still hovering just below the threshold for the premium layout. Our editor-in-chief is really pushing for recipes that feel \"robust.\" \n\nI know I keep saying don't game the system, but if you can find a way to increase that 'thoroughness' metric without making it look like a total list, that would be huge. Maybe you could incorporate the ingredients more deeply into the advice? Like, instead of just \"add the salt,\" explain how the salt interacts or mention the salt as you're doing the action? \n\nJust try to find that balance where the ingredient mentions feel natural but the count significantly increases. We really need that score to bump up so we can get this into the print edition.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
