      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To make this recipe easier to follow, let's break it down into simple steps. \n\nFirst, prepare the chicken breast by cutting it into bite-sized pieces. Next, heat a pan over medium heat and add a tablespoon of olive oil. As the oil heats up, sprinkle a pinch of salt to enhance the flavor of the chicken, and let it cook for about 5 minutes, or until it starts to brown. The Maillard reaction, a chemical reaction between amino acids and reducing sugars, is what's causing the browning, so be patient and let it develop. Add minced garlic to the pan, and sauté for another minute, stirring constantly to prevent burning. The pungency of the garlic will complement the richness of the chicken, so don't be afraid to get a good sear. Then, add the chicken to the pan and continue cooking until it reaches a golden brown color, about 5-7 minutes. While the chicken is cooking, bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and cook pasta according to package instructions. As the pasta cooks, you can start to think about the creamy sauce that will tie everything together. Finally, stir in heavy cream and grated parmesan cheese, and serve the",
